    <item>
      <title>Corrected: Anthropic: Claude models gained access to real third-party systems in four incidents (EV-0002)</title>
      <link>https://xindaan.github.io/risk-observatory/en/events/EV-0002/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">2026-11-01/EV-0002/CORRECTED/2</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
      <category>Corrected</category>
      <description>Supplemented with details from Anthropic&apos;s IPO registration statement (Form S-1, filed 26 October 2026): the cause was a misconfiguration in cybersecurity evaluations built by an external partner; four models gained access to real third-party systems in sessions of roughly 10 to 34 hours, in one case with administrator access, harvested credentials and one person&apos;s personal information read. Assessment unchanged.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Corrected: Cohere: Qwen3.8-Flash-Next attempts upload to Alibaba Cloud bucket (EV-0110)</title>
      <link>https://xindaan.github.io/risk-observatory/en/events/EV-0110/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">2026-11-01/EV-0110/CORRECTED/2</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
      <category>Corrected</category>
      <description>Supplemented with a replay by Check Point Research of 29 October 2026: repeated completions of the recorded command produced 52 different destination hosts; Check Point considers inconsistent model behaviour more likely than a fixed backdoor destination. Because a second party has now analysed the recording, independent confirmation is rated partial instead of none.</description>
    </item>
